Hello World!

This repo doubles as a tiny "Hello World" for Firecrawl (https://firecrawl.dev)
— turning any web page into clean, LLM-ready Markdown with a couple of lines of
Python.

Quickstart
----------

  1. Install the dependency:

       pip install -r requirements.txt

  2. Set your API key (get one at https://firecrawl.dev):

       cp .env.example .env        # then edit, or just:
       export FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=fc-...

  3. Run the example:

       python hello_firecrawl.py                       # scrape this repo's page
       python hello_firecrawl.py scrape https://example.com
       python hello_firecrawl.py search "Hello World site:github.com"

What it does
------------

hello_firecrawl.py wraps two Firecrawl endpoints:

  * scrape  — fetch a single URL and return its Markdown (firecrawl.scrape)
  * search  — search the web and list the top results (firecrawl.search)

Learn more in the Firecrawl docs: https://docs.firecrawl.dev
